    {
      "id": "38d0bf85-12e6-4e78-885a-cd62d0290ab5",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -760,
        -380
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 640,
        "height": 820,
        "content": "## Run an SMS campaign from Google Sheets and track delivery in the sheet\n\n### How it works\n1. Reads your contacts from a Google Sheet and keeps only rows with an empty **status**.\n2. Removes opted-out numbers with the SMS Vert Pro STOP list (`get_blacklist`) and marks them **OPTED_OUT**.\n3. Personalizes the message with `{firstname}` and checks it with `count_sms_parts`: texts with emojis or unsupported characters are marked **REJECTED_CHARACTERS** instead of failing at send time.\n4. Sends each SMS with `send_sms`, writes **SENT**, the campaign ID and the time back to the sheet.\n5. Waits one minute, fetches the delivery report and writes **DELIVERED**, **REJECTED**... in the **delivery** column.\n\n### Setup steps\n1. Create a sheet with the columns `phone`, `firstname`, `status`, `campaign_id`, `sent_at`, `delivery`. Phone numbers in international format without + (e.g. 33XXXXXXXXX for a French mobile).\n2. Connect your Google account in the Google Sheets nodes.\n3. Create a **Bearer Auth** credential with your SMS Vert Pro API V2 token (log in at smsvertpro.com, then open https://www.smsvertpro.com/api/doc-v2.php) and select it in the MCP Client nodes.\n4. In **Campaign settings**, paste your sheet URL, your sender name (11 characters max) and your message. **opt_out_mention** is added at the end of each SMS: \"STOP 36173\" is the opt-out short code required in France for marketing SMS (not a personal number); clear it for transactional messages.\n\n### Customization\nReplace the manual trigger with a Schedule Trigger to send at a fixed time, or add a column to target a segment. Run it again at any time: rows already processed are skipped."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
